-- First-constituent index over the AUTHORITATIVE trajectory geometry.
--
-- Answers "which composed entities begin with this child" as a range scan. For text the
-- first constituent is the first codepoint, so this is what makes a first-letter browse
-- possible without rendering a single name -- the access path constituent_edges was
-- reaching for, done as an index instead of a hand-refreshed copy. Postgres maintains it
-- on write, transactionally; there is nothing to regenerate and nothing that can go stale.
--
-- Built on laplace_trajectory_constituent_ids, which has shipped in laplace_geom since the
-- beginning and is IMMUTABLE. That matters for more than convenience: laplace_geom is
-- pinned at its project version with no upgrade script, so a function ADDED to it never
-- reaches an already-installed database -- and an index expression is evaluated immediately
-- at CREATE INDEX, so it hard-fails rather than degrading. Depending only on what geom
-- already exports keeps this substrate upgrade self-contained.
--
-- Scoped to type = 1 (the canonical content physicality a composed entity's constituents
-- are decoded from) and to rows that carry a trajectory, so the index covers only what it
-- can answer for.
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS physicalities_traj_first_id_btree
    ON physicalities (((public.laplace_trajectory_constituent_ids(trajectory))[1]))
    WHERE trajectory IS NOT NULL AND type = 1;
